@startuml sequence-diagram-auth
/'
  AI Usage Note
  Drafted with Claude from the code and authentication.md.
'/
title Nearby — Sequence Diagram: Registration, Sign-in and Access Tokens

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor "Client\n(app, Swagger UI)" as APP
box "api" #F5F5F5
  participant "AuthController\n+ AuthGuard" as API
end box
box "core: identity" #EEF4FB
  participant "AuthService" as SVC
end box
box "infra (behind core interfaces)" #F3F8EE
  database "VerificationCodes\nRepository" as CODES
  database "Accounts\nRepository" as ACC
  participant "CodeHasher (HMAC)\nPasswordHasher (argon2id)" as HASH
  participant "AccessTokens\n(jose, HS256)" as TOK
  participant "MessagingProvider\n(via core notifications)" as MSG
end box

== Register: request a code ==

APP -> API : POST /auth/register {phone}
API -> SVC : register(phone)
SVC -> CODES : findLatest(phone)
alt a code was sent less than a minute ago
  SVC --> APP : 429 CODE_RESEND_TOO_SOON
end
SVC -> SVC : random 6-digit code
SVC -> HASH : HMAC(phone:code)
SVC -> CODES : create(hash, expires in 10 min)
SVC -> MSG : sendCode(phone, code)
note right of MSG : now: logged to the console;\nlater: Telegram Gateway → SMS
API --> APP : 202 — same answer for a registered phone

== Verify: finish registration ==

APP -> API : POST /auth/verify {phone, code, password, dateOfBirth}
API -> SVC : verify(…)
SVC -> CODES : findLatest(phone)
alt no code, expired, used or 3 failed attempts
  SVC --> APP : 422 INVALID_CODE
else HMAC does not match
  SVC -> CODES : addFailedAttempt
  SVC --> APP : 422 INVALID_CODE
end
SVC -> CODES : markUsed — false if another request used it first
SVC -> SVC : age ≥ 18 by the Kyiv date
alt under 18
  SVC --> APP : 422 UNDERAGE
else phone already registered
  SVC --> APP : 409 CONFLICT
end
SVC -> HASH : argon2id(password)
SVC -> ACC : create(account, passwordHash)
SVC -> TOK : issue(account caller, 3600 s)
API --> APP : 200 {accessToken, expiresIn: 3600}

== Sign in ==

APP -> API : POST /auth/sign-in {phone, password}
API -> SVC : signIn(phone, password)
SVC -> ACC : findPasswordCredential(phone)
SVC -> HASH : verify(hash, password)\n— a dummy hash for an unknown phone
alt unknown phone, wrong password or banned
  SVC --> APP : 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS — does not say which
end
SVC -> TOK : issue(account caller, 3600 s)
API --> APP : 200 {accessToken, expiresIn: 3600}

== Guest token ==

APP -> API : POST /auth/guest
API -> SVC : issueGuestToken()
SVC -> TOK : issue(guest caller with a random id)
API --> APP : 200 {accessToken}

== Any protected request ==

APP -> API : GET /api/v1/… — Authorization: Bearer <token>
API -> SVC : authenticate(token)
SVC -> TOK : verify(token)
TOK -> TOK : key by kid; HS256 only; signature;\niss, aud, typ at+jwt; not expired;\nclaims parsed into a Caller
alt any check fails
  API --> APP : 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
else guest on a user endpoint
  API --> APP : 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
else user on an admin endpoint
  API --> APP : 404 NOT_FOUND
end
API -> API : handler runs with the Caller

note over APP, MSG
  Errors: AuthService throws a DomainError with a code; ApiExceptionFilter (api) turns it into the status shown.
  Token: header {alg HS256, kid, typ at+jwt}; claims sub, role, sid (accounts only), iss/aud nearby-api, iat, exp.
  Keys: JWT_KEYS_FILE (JWK Set, first key signs) and CODE_HMAC_KEY_FILE, read at startup; a missing or short key stops the server.
  Planned, not shown: refresh tokens and a revocation check by sid (SEC-005), lockout and rate limits (SEC-007), audit records (SEC-004).
end note
@enduml
